From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Braga <brunobraga@google.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:14:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/48] [Autofill AI] Block primary order/shipment suggestions
 in cross-origin iframes

Previously, `IsAllowedForPageUrl` only checked whether an `kOrder` or
`kShipment` entity's domain matched the primary main frame URL via PSL
matching (`client.GetLastCommittedPrimaryMainFrameURL()`), without
verifying the origin of the triggering field's frame. As a result, a
cross-origin iframe embedded in a merchant or carrier page could receive
primary top-level order/shipment suggestions for that merchant/carrier.

This CL aligns `IsAllowedForPageUrl` with the domain-gating logic used
for loyalty cards (`ValuableSuggestionGenerator`).

Bug: 540020706
Change-Id: I4bde214f33791e6a147bcbb3c502c2cbd4669da5
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549773
